diff --git a/docs/src/config/ini-config.adoc b/docs/src/config/ini-config.adoc
index de598c529d..cdb1333971 100644
--- a/docs/src/config/ini-config.adoc
+++ b/docs/src/config/ini-config.adoc
@@ -1210,6 +1210,30 @@ These parameters are Homing related, for a better explanation read the <<cha:hom
 * `VOLATILE_HOME = 0` - (bool)
   When enabled (set to `1`) this joint will be unhomed if the Machine Power is off or if E-Stop is on.
   This is useful if your machine has home switches and does not have position feedback such as a step and direction driven machine.
+* `AVAILABILITY_CONTROL = 0` - (bool)
+  Enables acquisition and release of the joint through HAL `availability-request`
+  and `availability-ack` pins. Extra joints (`num_extrajoints`) are unsupported.
+  When disabled, the joint uses normal activation and rejects availability commands.
+  A controlled joint always starts released and must be acquired after Machine On.
+  An availability-controlled joint must not define `HOME_SEQUENCE`. Home All
+  skips unavailable controlled joints, and ordinary individual home commands
+  for controlled joints are rejected.
+* `AVAILABILITY_TIMEOUT = 5.0` - (real)
+  Maximum wait for hardware acknowledgment, in seconds. Must be finite and greater than zero.
+
+Releasing a joint freezes its logical joint and Cartesian position while the raw
+HAL feedback pin remains live. Acquisition individually homes any unhomed joint
+and publishes it as available only after homing succeeds. If the joint is
+already homed, acquisition verifies physical feedback against the held position
+using the joint's minimum following-error tolerance; a mismatch faults without
+changing the held position. `VOLATILE_HOME = 1` only controls whether release
+invalidates that reference. Other motion is allowed only if it leaves
+unavailable joints at their held command positions. Released joints do not
+require homing to permit Run or MDI.
+
+NML/Python commands acquire and release resources while the task is idle.
+Only one operation may be pending; use Abort to cancel it. Completion waits for
+the hardware handshake and either required homing or held-position validation.
 
 ==== Servos
 
@@ -1450,6 +1474,13 @@ Control screens can limit these settings further.
 * `HOME_SEQUENCE = 0` - (int) FIXME: Spindle homing not yet working
   Controls where in the general homing sequence the spindle homing rotations occur.
   Set the `HOME_SEARCH_VELOCITY` to zero to avoid spindle rotation during the homing sequence.
+* `AVAILABILITY_CONTROL = 0` - (bool)
+  Enables runtime acquisition and release of this physical spindle resource.
+* `INITIAL_AVAILABILITY =` `0` | `1` - (bool)
+  Required when `AVAILABILITY_CONTROL = 1`.
+  Set to `1` to acquire the spindle on Machine On, or `0` to leave it released.
+* `AVAILABILITY_TIMEOUT = 5.0` - (real)
+  Maximum wait for hardware acknowledgment, in seconds. Must be finite and greater than zero.
 
