new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..bdfd8cc4e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/runtime-availability/README
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+Userspace POSIX simulation: actual target enforcement, released-joint MDI eligibility, late ACK cancellation, held-position validation, and homing abort cleanup.
+Cancellation waits for actual homing velocity and checks stationary completion and reacquisition.
+Direct admission rejects dwell/queued MDI and paused AUTO, overlaps (including no-ops and other resources), and interpretation/jogging before completion. With forced homing enabled, Home All skips unavailable controlled joints, first acquisition homes an unhomed nonvolatile joint, and controlled joints reject user HOME/UNHOME outside acquisition. Later nonvolatile acquisition preserves a matching held position and rejects changed or non-finite feedback without publishing availability. Volatile acquisition accepts arbitrary unavailable movement only through successful homing. Abort during ACK wait and moving homing cannot be revived by late ACK; later reacquisition succeeds.
+
+INI fixtures are generated by test.sh from the shared FIXTURE.BASE and local
+*.ini.in overrides. Run python3 ../runtime-availability/make-fixtures.py before
+launching an individual case directly. @unset explicitly removes an inherited
+key. Generated INIs are ignored; edit the base or the case override instead.
